@startuml PayLink_Payment_State_Diagram
top to bottom direction
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 50

state Initiated
state FundsHeld
state Rejected
state SentToBiller
state Completed
state Failed
state Unknown
state Refunded

[*] --> Initiated

Initiated --> FundsHeld : validatePayment\n[fraud checks pass &\nwallet has enough funds]
Initiated --> Rejected : validatePayment\n[fraud check fails or\ninsufficient funds]

FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : dispatchPayment\n[request sent to biller]

SentToBiller --> Completed : billerResponse\n[biller confirms]
SentToBiller --> Failed : billerResponse\n[biller refuses]
SentToBiller --> Unknown : billerTimeout\n[no answer within 10s timeout]

Unknown --> Completed : statusResolved\n[biller later confirms via\ncallback, retry, or settlement file]
Unknown --> Failed : statusResolved\n[biller later refuses or\nreconciliation finds no payment]

Failed --> Refunded : releaseHold\n[hold released to wallet]

Rejected --> [*]
Completed --> [*]
Refunded --> [*]

note right of Unknown
  Funds remain held; never
  refunded automatically.
  Re-queried up to 3 times
  (after 1, 5, and 15 minutes),
  then awaits nightly reconciliation.
end note

note left of Completed
  Final state. Post-completion
  refunds (FR-27) use a separate
  RefundRequest entity and are
  not a state transition.
end note
@enduml